# Wealth Blotter Plus — Core

## Stack

- Python 3.10+, FastAPI, Pydantic v2, CrewAI (local Ollama by default; cloud LLMs via env flags)
- Supabase (PostgreSQL + RLS) for persistence and audit logging
- Frontends: `frontend_excel/` (Office.js + Vite) and `frontend_streamlit/`

## Layout (domain isolation)

```
/backend
  /app/api          HTTP routers
  /app/core         JWT, Supabase clients, rules cache
  /app/schemas      Immutable Pydantic contracts
  /app/agents       CrewAI, tools, YAML, self-healing
  /app/db           SQL DDL, RLS, seeds, seed_configs
/frontend_excel     Vite + Office.js task pane
/frontend_streamlit Ops & agent debug dashboard
```

Keep parallel agents inside one tree at a time.

## Architecture

- **Self-healing:** On Pydantic/JSON errors from CrewAI, feed the trace back into agent context and retry up to 3 times
- **Confidence routing:** Parse `confidence_score` (0.0–1.0); `≥ 0.85` → blotter staging; `< 0.85` → HITL review
- **Accuracy audit:** Persist agent output vs advisor-saved output in `agent_output_reviews`
- **Config split:** `technical_limits` vs `business_guardrails` in Supabase `configs` (jsonb) — never mix; seed from `backend/app/db/seed_configs/`
- **LLM defaults:** Global temperature `0.2` in `config.py`; per-agent overrides in `agents.yaml`

## Contracts & parallel work

- Treat Pydantic models, FastAPI OpenAPI schemas, and SQL DDL as immutable contracts
- One agent owns a file tree at a time; changes must be self-contained, typed, and testable before integration

## Audit

- Route execution events, API requests, confidence metrics, and validation errors to Supabase `audit_logs` (immutable)
